-This method selects a valid, cache-resident resolution level for volume rendering when the desired resolution is not available in the cache [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of missing data bricks by iteratively searching for alternative resolutions based on a node's residency bitmap, prioritizing lower resolutions before higher ones [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Finding Higher Resolution Levels](5315-finding-higher-resolution-levels.md) by its primary search direction (lower first) and from [Hierarchical Culling & Multi-resolution Approximation](2010-hierarchical-culling-multi-resolution-approximation.md) by relying on explicit bitmap masks rather than error metrics for selection.
+This method selects a valid, cache-resident resolution level for volume rendering when the desired resolution is not available in the cache [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of missing data bricks by iteratively searching for alternative resolutions based on a node's residency bitmap, prioritizing lower resolutions before higher ones [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods by using explicit bitwise masks on a node's partial-mapping state to filter candidates before performing cache lookups, avoiding exhaustive searches [S1, unofficial].
 
